Hey, guys -
Would like to thank you for the new flight simulator! It is GREAT and a huge improvement from Flight School. There is definitely room for improvements, which is expected for a brand new simulator, so I have no complaints. However, I would like to provide a  few suggestions after playing it to hopefully help out:
1. More functionality and accuracy of the G1000;
2. Offer more information in the POH section;
3. ATC transmitions to be more accurate;
4. Be able to hear transmitions between ATC and Pilot (had a voice selected, but was still not able to hear anything).
Again, great job! It is appreciated. I have only played it once, so I will offer more suggestions once I become more familiar with it.
Dillon

Finally someone did a true Magic: The Gathering / Hearthstone mix!
I'm an old time MtG player (think 1998) and Hearthstone legend player, and I admit the game looks really fun.
Here's what became apparent after a few games:
Hearthstone influence:
- battlegrounds look and feel the same;
- lots of battlecry ("summon") & deathrattle ("entomb") effects;
- hero weapons.
MTG influence:
- untargetted attacks, blocks made by defender;
- You have lands ("sigils");
- creatures are healed at end of turn;
- flying, trample ("overwhelm");
- instant effects (played in other player's turn);
- MTG-style mulligan.
P.S. I love the fact that you can use A for attack-all, wish Hearthstone had something like this!

I don't think DS2 is a bad game by itself. It has enough innovation and some decent new mechanics to keep DS1 veterans interested for a large amount of time. But comparing it to its predecessor I see a lot of really annoying design decisions. So many, in fact, that, even after putting so much effort into it, I won't be finishing it.
My personal aggravations, to name a few:
* inability to skip or run through unwanted fights;
* having to grind out the paths to the bosses instead of just opening a shortcut;
* ruined cast times;
* recycled bosses and boss mechanics;
* forced invasions.

